6. What safety or auto-repair features would you build into .hfz to keep your code healthy and running smooth?

I would build the Guardian Protocol, an automated immune system for our code.

Principle of Reversibility: Every action in .hfz is transactional. A bad deploy? hfz rollback --last. A corrupted database migration? hfz revert --transaction <id>. There is always an undo button.

Auto-Immune Response: The system constantly monitors its own production health. If it detects a security vulnerability or anomalous behavior, it automatically isolates the component (like a digital quarantine), deploys the last known good version, and creates a high-priority "Bounty" ticket with all the diagnostic data for the team to address.

